## Context
The subcommands of `scripts/zotero.py` carry unspecific names (`probe`,
`match`, `audit`, `attach`, `inject`, `enrich`, `write`); the author asked for
names that say what each does (2026-10-16). `probe` also does two unrelated
things: it extracts metadata from a PDF and looks the work up in the library.

Blocked by 1113 (PR #1441): it rewrites the same script, tests and docs to read
through the Zotero local API only.

## Author decisions (2026-10-16)
- Rename the subcommands to specific names; the proposed table below was
  approved ("better").
- Split `probe`: "Extracting is different than looking up. For example,
  extracting is input format dependant, while looking up is a local API call
  (ensuring it is available, stateless, never direct sqlite, never web)."
  - `extract-metadata`: input-format dependent (PDF today), never needs Zotero.
  - `find-work`: library lookup through the local API only; ensures Zotero is
    available (launch it or do nothing), stateless, never sqlite, never web.
    It absorbs `match` and takes the extracted metadata as input.

| Now | Does | New |
|---|---|---|
| `probe` | extract PDF metadata + library lookup | split: `extract-metadata`, `find-work` |
| `match` | look a work up from given metadata | `find-work` |
| `dedup-report` | read-only report of duplicate items | `report-duplicates` |
| `audit` | compare a `docs/` staging directory with the library | `check-staging-dir` |
| `reconcile` | compare `.bib`-linked staging files with the library | `check-bib-staging` |
| `attach` | report how to file documents onto an existing item | `suggest-attachments` |
| `write` | write a RIS file from JSON entries | `write-ris` |
| `inject` | create items + PDFs through the desktop connector | `create-items` |
| `enrich` | report missing fields on existing items | `suggest-edits` |

## Author decisions (2026-10-16, "oui à tout")
Proposed after a size review of `scripts/zotero.py` (3,051 lines once PR #1441
lands, -4% from main despite the pyzotero swap); the author accepted all five:
1. Merge `audit` and `reconcile` into one command with two input modes (a
   `docs/` directory, or the files linked from `.bib` entries).
2. Replace the in-memory duplicate cascade (`library_matches`,
   `_library_views`, `corroborate`, `_surname_in_text`,
   `entry_identity_keys`) with Zotero's own search through the local API
   (`q`, `qmode=everything`; present in Zotero 10's `server_localAPI.js`) for
   DOI, ISBN and title, plus `rapidfuzz` for title similarity. No whole-library
   read per call.
3. Drop RIS writing (`write`, `entry_to_ris`): items are created in Zotero
   directly. Update `rules/zotero.md` where it says to archive "RIS +
   attachment".
4. Drop the HTML output of `dedup-report`; JSON only.
5. Evaluate `pdf2doi` for finding a PDF's own DOI, offline only; adopt it only
   if it never touches the web, else keep the current extraction.

## Author decisions (2026-10-16, "oui oui oui", from the /gaze of PR #1441)
6. Accept only "Always Allow" local keys; delete the one-time-key path.
7. Zotero 10 or later is the floor for the whole helper (local writes need it
   already); drop the Zotero 7-9 attachment-file branch instead of testing it.
8. A slow or timed-out library read is a visible failure, distinct from
   "Zotero unavailable": an unattended reconcile must not exit 0 on it.

## Author decisions (2026-10-16, "Oui pour tout")
9. Cut the hand-rolled match scoring: `find-work` and every caller return
   Zotero's local-API search results per key (DOI, ISBN, arXiv/handle,
   title), and the only match the helper asserts is EXACT equality of a
   normalised identifier against the hit's own field. Delete rapidfuzz title
   scoring, `corroborate` and its rebuild, the ±3-year rule, and any
   verification/scorer layer; title hits are returned as candidates for the
   author or calling agent to judge, never auto-matched. Remove rapidfuzz
   from dependencies if nothing else needs it. Keep the safety property that
   a cited work's DOI is never attached to the wrong item: with
   exact-identifier-only matching and no auto-match on titles, state in the
   PR body how that property now holds (or what is lost).
   (Supersedes the rapidfuzz half of decision 2.)
10. The merged command name `check-staging` is approved.
11. Replace the entry `type` RIS codes with Zotero item types (the previous
    worker estimated ~40 lines removed); RIS is gone, so the RIS vocabulary
    goes too. Update the entry contract docs.

Standing order: "sans réinventer la roue": before keeping any hand-rolled
piece, use pyzotero/Zotero for it; report `scripts/zotero.py` line counts
before (3,005 at 497b2b7c) and after, with a one-line justification for
each kept hand-rolled piece.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `probe` is replaced by `extract-metadata` (no Zotero access) and `find-work` (local API only); extraction output feeds the lookup
- [ ] Every subcommand carries its new name; no alias for the old names (`check-staging` approved)
- [ ] `skills/zotero/`, `skills/lair/` (the `/zotero reconcile` proposal), `rules/zotero.md`, docs and README use only the new names
- [ ] Tests cover the split: extraction runs with Zotero down; lookup does nothing when Zotero is unavailable
- [ ] `audit` and `reconcile` are one command with two input modes
- [ ] Duplicate lookup uses Zotero's local-API search per key; no whole-library read per call
- [ ] The only asserted match is exact equality of a normalised identifier against the hit's own field; title hits are candidates, never auto-matched
- [ ] No rapidfuzz title scoring, no `corroborate` (nor its rebuild), no ±3-year rule, no scorer layer; rapidfuzz gone from the dependencies if nothing else needs it
- [ ] PR body states how "a cited work's DOI is never attached to the wrong item" now holds, or what is lost
- [ ] No RIS writer; `rules/zotero.md` no longer prescribes RIS archiving
- [ ] An entry's `type` is a Zotero item type; no RIS type code is left in the helper or the entry contract docs
- [ ] `dedup-report` (renamed) emits JSON only
- [ ] `pdf2doi` evaluated offline: adopted with no web access, or rejected with the reason in the PR body
- [ ] Before/after line counts of `scripts/zotero.py` reported; every kept hand-rolled piece justified
- [ ] Live tests keep the private-Xvfb fixture: no Zotero window on the author's display
- [ ] Only "Always Allow" keys; no one-time-key code
- [ ] Zotero 10 is the stated and enforced floor; no Zotero 7-9 branch
- [ ] A slow read fails visibly (own verdict, non-zero exit), never reported as unavailable
- [ ] `make check` passes
